ylPAAHBC7FrP2ZcV795DKt9XvdmriQ-VFgV6nsadf2uSGSS_V8r-YEYFdhCGWnqaxBiziGA_7qWwqbjzPfXGjfOyGNWjV-byTHKo5Wcowst3enzjJZcIzB9mDpDic1wdXelsQMtgzkh0Nvn1BFsHkJ6tMuPYRUPR_-e5zash6oJm_MFjc1QF81wr5lCFjoz83fQPGQIj76A9w3K51K9_K6KZO8W7VfhNquGyRXPiHF3NPY5UMiEVrLFkUcuCUHn8l5D9bmqfqprbu88kjpzYlKJezWDtaiVMkDrrHpzLeiAoDXAPIJ4MIBK83G0UYwQJ1TAAchIYhArNAZUxlovxxD6tnjY2RKBgM1-bve54J_EpizDP_fbrKe6xYn0PdCmccOIKUf78k1LcaFWCZ77jJ6W0J3VjYMX2s8kVm0m5-RiKDpbK5-EGiNqWOxjkunNVDsVq611lIGwPM6t30iRWmkaDxPw5IUJAaQ2NIi_8kregnUiGAYhVfmfbn9e2IW25-h8mVv2s9geHc8V0XxydN8c1i7_C2Uu-5I=\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Structuring medical response**\\n\\nI need to create a medical first response structure since the user mentioned an EHR DNA report, which suggests I should apply the patient-klm skill. I think I must present one skill upfront: patient-klm. Although I have prior work or patient data, it seems I should focus on this current conversation. I need to ask five questions one at a time, starting with the diagnosis output structure and mentioning that answering all five can help. I’ll give the first question only. I should also mention that patient-klm could be used to retrieve information.\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_Qr1Jl7vMAgMq4yvqCXMZRuXP|fc_0208e2a9d48ad22f0169bbd66a85048191b9cc5a3e790ed480","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/SKILL.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/SKILL.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":2702,"output":157,"cacheRead":9472,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":12331,"cost":{"input":0.006755000000000001,"output":0.002355,"cacheRead":0.002368,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.011478}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773917796408}}
{"type":"message","id":"827140e8","parentId":"ec9de140","timestamp":"2026-03-19T10:56:42.634Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Qr1Jl7vMAgMq4yvqCXMZRuXP|fc_0208e2a9d48ad22f0169bbd66a85048191b9cc5a3e790ed480","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: patient-klm\ndescription: Access and update a patient-specific knowledge store backed by a Patient KLM API that exposes EHR records, disease timelines, genomic profiles, and custom structured triples in SQLite. Use when a user asks to retrieve, inspect, summarize, add, or update patient knowledge base data; fetch patient context for agent personalization; view all triples for a patient; inspect the disease timeline; inspect genomics; create a new patient; add a visit; or add a custom triple. Default to patient_id `P-001` when the user asks for patient knowledge base access without specifying a patient. If the intended endpoint is unclear, ask a brief clarification question before writing data.\n---\n\n# Patient KLM\n\nUse this skill to read from or write to the Patient KLM API at `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:8006`.\n\n## Quick routing\n\nMap the user request to exactly one endpoint when possible:\n\n- **Get all patient triples / patient record / patient knowledge base** → `GET /patient/{patient_id}`\n- **Get progression / disease course / timeline / labs over time / imaging over time** → `GET /patient/{patient_id}/timeline`\n- **Get DNA / genomics / variants / genetic profile** → `GET /patient/{patient_id}/genomics`\n- **Create a new patient** → `POST /patient`\n- **Add a clinic visit / new appointment / follow-up encounter** → `POST /patient/{patient_id}/visit`\n- **Add custom fact / family history / social history / risk factor / arbitrary triple** → `POST /triple`\n\nIf the user does not specify a patient for a read request, use `P-001`.\n\nIf the user asks for “access the knowledge base” but does not say *what* they want from it, ask a short clarification question such as:\n- “Do you want the full patient record, the timeline, or the genomics profile?”\n\n## Default behavior\n\n- Prefer the helper script: `scripts/patient_klm_api.py`\n- Resolve that path from the current skill directory or use the current user's absolute path: `~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py`\n- Do **not** use `/root/.openclaw/...` paths; they may be unreadable when the runtime user is not root.\n- For read requests, return the API result and summarize it if the user appears to want interpretation.\n- For write requests, confirm only when the request is ambiguous or materially incomplete. Do not add data that the user did not provide.\n- Preserve user-provided field names and values exactly unless the API rejects them.\n\n## Use the helper script\n\nRun from the skill directory or pass the absolute path for the **current user**.\n\n### Read patient data\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm && python3 scripts/patient_klm_api.py get-patient --patient-id P-001\ncd ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm && python3 scripts/patient_klm_api.py get-timeline --patient-id P-001\ncd ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm && python3 scripts/patient_klm_api.py get-genomics --patient-id P-001\n```\n\nOr, with an explicit safe absolute path:\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py get-patient --patient-id P-001\npython3 ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py get-timeline --patient-id P-001\npython3 ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py get-genomics --patient-id P-001\n```\n\nIf `--patient-id` is omitted for read commands, the script defaults to `P-001`.\n\n### Create or update patient data\n\nPass JSON inline or via a file.\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py add-patient --json '{\"patient_id\":\"P-002\",\"name\":\"John Smith\"}'\npython3 ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py add-visit --patient-id P-001 --json '{\"visit_date\":\"2026-03-10\",\"symptoms\":[\"fatigue\"]}'\npython3 ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py add-triple --json '{\"patient_id\":\"P-001\",\"head\":\"P-001\",\"relation\":\"has_risk_factor\",\"tail\":\"smoking:20_pack_years\"}'\n```\n\nOr:\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/patient_klm_api.py add-patient --file payload.json\n```\n\n## Required data by operation\n\n### `POST /patient`\nMinimum required fields:\n- `patient_id`\n- `name`\n\nOptional fields include demographics, baseline conditions, a first visit, and genomic variants.\n\n### `POST /patient/{patient_id}/visit`\nRequire:\n- `patient_id`\n- visit payload JSON\n\nCommon visit fields:\n- `visit_date`\n- `symptoms`\n- `vitals`\n- `lab_results`\n- `diagnosis_codes`\n- `medications`\n- `imaging`\n- `clinical_notes`\n\n### `POST /triple`\nRequire a JSON body containing at least the triple identity fields expected by the API, typically:\n- `patient_id`\n- `head`\n- `relation`\n- `tail`\n\nOptional metadata may include:\n- `confidence`\n- `evidence_level`\n- `source`\n- `timestamp`\n\n## Response handling\n\n- If the API returns JSON, surface the key result cleanly.\n- If a read response is large, summarize the main findings and offer the raw JSON on request.\n- If a write succeeds, report what was added.\n- If the API returns an error, quote the status and response body briefly so the user can correct the request.\n\n## Files\n\n- Helper script: `scripts/patient_klm_api.py`\n- API reference: `references/api.md`\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773917802629}}
{"type":"message","id":"6d7a1f5e","parentId":"827140e8","timestamp":"2026-03-19T10:57:00.866Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Fetching patient data**\n\nI think I need to use exec to get the patient data, along with genomics and a timeline, since the user mentioned it's already been sent. It seems like a good idea to fetch all this information in parallel, possibly by using a multi-tool approach. I could also consider calling three Python scripts sequentially with bash for this. It feels like I should keep the narration brief for clarity.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0208e2a9d48ad22f0169bbd66c2f9c81919699a4e02d55467e\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpu9ZwM56_jxdZX9k_9SpFADUvREKWYbbatYWxndIvqrPsV4C-NifjsIxOw6_i_CS2FV3SDyn9uYUVD3It94s2_UOFOuvbcf85AWRfmZn1I_JNVTe_o8BrMst1t3pO5NCHDEwVG4P-nHMePSRHYtABpRnIzgZ12P9aKf3z6etTyVh5sCitHwGhTnLfEumtZtBR5KqBSoKjv4BtR1qtFJI4juJHyAT4JyhVmnHX8EPIsFFlZ6NLmS_s6O4kYTr4yHlsHjPt7d4x3oH80AO0Z7jvFTDWFI55NMvX-_P0jnGKwROHgn5kOrKShZnZnTZypXRrrGg30KB2ywyCYye1ePKLHNDXHLa1Dbs_crksfRWTSJc2GHiG_0PPgtBdF6_VSC8zh4ufbzOXCKubjTg8EqWxzYcdinxVKZyRltr6kf2sJFIZTNIzVqT1G-y02TEunudS0CJREcLmdB3cHPiEFuRs0UTdYRHUg8Uy33aXMcYmSm9T6kFeIzg3IwHGrmnBLOZCdbISBUkd9o0hBPeT58cIXwdUa_dp9KlBh8a6Asvh2tfYXHw02Bu-Xk6vvD27Njt2XbI21jrJ9TFIoXx38tVN0lH9Mu5TvFrg1hJSGbkhnCp1UEFCnBAS3hZhMnpw4xiCmNvfzjavL7Z5qucFDZkzXNC7-4QzVPUvWVLmwNbFg6FkeRdlyudF07Q1asllP3tk4C8J0g2eo6g6dGG8CA-Wxk8CYUL5trmYq7QSe8SulK6Z9EbpXQwpOdSIESqgvNvlQs9pplh7CpBmH8gQDI_HBzKJ2kdP3_dyE7bJx-Bp9QJaHoJNnoqjQ7r3ue4_YYsQWuzEdRDCa1hnKwEIwBsXC2xFH7pnh52EEzm3GBtl6b-DqM8MKZ5g2Vz0ssGlpB8XoofBmykjyGc7jwJ4fLRxxRUpBW1dYT-6yTUnlh6jXH18_-JFyV_QvbGqv2wNDdBeO6hqHVS75JzKr5VzGbBQq9RGrWv5LEPBhejvZ5XypcjFWXU59rtrkAo31WcMZqiTeKhHVYiBFiv6GH0dyo5KZMgbNRZY-y84GFgEAM6VUIQb5De-x02XKHlO32N4f99U7uLCwRSKTWJ7WGMzw1HeSK7eLMdsMFw4681KKYlINg2zcytdzFmfYjnTDCcmyK3C_EtV4Q_xcJhLgVKDkLeOAahxNzRdLrTu5kQMt_rFqHaUIZCAj40hFIpHXCjKrjM59AV8\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Fetching patient data**\\n\\nI think I need to use exec to get the patient data, along with genomics and a timeline, since the user mentioned it's already been sent. It seems like a good idea to fetch all this information in parallel, possibly by using a multi-tool approach. I could also consider calling three Python scripts sequentially with bash for this. It feels like I should keep the narration brief for clarity.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"I’m going to pull your stored record and genomics context so I can tie your current symptoms to what’s already on file.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0208e2a9d48ad22f0169bbd67047408191b2b80f1e5081b07e\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_XJubaprHLxidrhJ43E3Ljn0W|fc_0208e2a9d48ad22f0169bbd67cc91c8191a604b6c0a826c376","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py get-patient --patient-id P-001","workdir":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent","yieldMs":10000},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py get-patient --patient-id P-001\",\"workdir\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent\",\"yieldMs\":10000}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2D9og2aZWt9JQDDfx8xAwAnS|fc_0208e2a9d48ad22f0169bbd67cc93081919de7923a9112e28e","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py get-timeline --patient-id P-001","workdir":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent","yieldMs":10000},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py get-timeline --patient-id P-001\",\"workdir\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent\",\"yieldMs\":10000}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_id5HbHotLXH0ZwiDeBKBDp7I|fc_0208e2a9d48ad22f0169bbd67cc9388191be3a564ec1455d1a","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py get-genomics --patient-id P